
# P3: Feature-Branch Git Workflow

## Aim
To implement a feature using a separate Git branch and merge it into the main branch.

## Commands and Implementation

### 1. Create and Switch to Feature Branch
```bash
git switch -c feature/about-section
```

### 2. Create a New File
```bash
touch about.html
```

### 3. Add Changes
```bash
git add .
```

### 4. Commit Changes
```bash
git commit -m "Add about section"
```

### 5. Switch to Main Branch
```bash
git switch main
```

### 6. Merge Feature Branch
```bash
git merge feature/about-section
```

### 7. View Branches
```bash
git branch
```

### 8. View Commit History
```bash
git log --oneline --graph
```

## Expected Output
The feature branch is successfully created and merged into the main branch.

## Result
Successfully implemented the feature-branch workflow using Git.
